      ],\n          \"urls\": [],\n          \"symbols\": []\n        },\n        \"card\": null,\n        \"poll\": null,\n        \"article\": null,\n        \"place\": null,\n        \"communityNote\": null,\n        \"isEdited\": false,\n        \"quotedTweet\": null,\n        \"retweetedTweet\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"2013769108253298877\",\n        \"url\": \"https://x.com/TweetsbyCoachP/status/2013769108253298877\",\n        \"text\": \"Players and Parents: Critical piece of recruiting advice from a current Athletic Director, former college basketball coach, and parent of 4 that played or participated in college….\\n\\nAsk this crucial question…..”would I attend that school if athletics weren’t involved at all?”\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-01-21T00:22:24.000Z\",\n        \"createdAtUnix\": 1768954944,\n        \"createdAtLabel\": null,\n        \"language\": \"en\",\n        \"conversationId\": \"2013769108253298877\",\n        \"inReplyToStatusId\": null,\n        \"inReplyToUserId\": null,\n        \"inReplyToScreenName\": null,\n        \"quotedStatusId\": null,\n        \"retweetTweetId\": null,\n        \"author\": {\n          \"handle\": \"TweetsbyCoachP\",\n          \"displayName\": \"William Payne\",\n          \"avatarUrl\": \"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2108037448278450176/xNRFLgTH_400x400.jpg\",\n          \"profileUrl\": \"https://x.com/TweetsbyCoachP\",\n          \"verified\": false,\n          \"blueVerified\": true,\n          \"platformUserId\": \"2542103608\",\n          \"bio\": \"Systemwide Director of Athletics @ Pinecrest Academies of Nevada •🏆 Winning Small College 🏀 Coach • Recruiting • Small College/HBCU Advocate • 📚📕📗📘📙\",\n          \"location\": \"Henderson, NV\",\n          \"website\": \"https://www.pinecrestnv.org/\",\n          \"bannerUrl\": \"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/2542103608/1787777405/1500x500\",\n          \"accountCreatedAt\": \"2014-05-12T00:43:06.000Z\",\n          \"privateAccount\": false,\n          \"verifiedType\": null,\n          \"affiliateLabel\": null,\n          \"professional\": {\n            \"type\": \"Creator\",\n            \"category\": [\n              {\n                \"id\": 800,\n                \"name\": \"Sports, Fitness & Recreation\",\n                \"icon_name\": \"IconBriefcaseStroke\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"restId\": \"1471870317882654720\"\n          },\n          \"metrics\": {\n            \"availableFields\": [\n              \"followers\",\n              \"following\",\n              \"tweets\",\n              \"favourites\",\n              \"listedCount\",\n              \"mediaCount\"\n            ],\n            \"followers\": 115986,\n            \"following\": 4599,\n            \"tweets\": 80052,\n            \"favourites\": 143639,\n            \"listedCount\": 108,\n            \"mediaCount\": 5203\n          }\n        },\n        \"metrics\": {\n          \"availableFields\": [\n            \"likes\",\n            \"retweets\",\n            \"replies\",\n            \"quotes\",\n            \"views\",\n            \"bookmarkCount\"\n          ],\n          \"likes\": 32,\n          \"retweets\": 5,\n          \"replies\": 2,\n          \"quotes\": 0,\n          \"views\": 4145,\n          \"bookmarkCount\": 1\n        },\n        \"media\": [],\n        \"expandedUrl\": null,\n        \"isRetweet\": false,\n        \"isReply\": false,\n        \"isQuote\": false,\n        \"source\": \"Twitter for iPhone\",\n        \"communityId\": null,\n        \"hasAIGeneratedMedia\": false,\n        \"isPaidPromotion\": false,\n        \"isTranslatable\": false,\n        \"hasBirdwatchNotes\": false,\n        \"possiblySensitive\": false,\n        \"entities\": {\n          \"hashtags\": [],\n          \"userMentions\": [],\n          \"urls\": [],\n          \"symbols\": []\n        },\n        \"card\": null,\n        \"poll\": null,\n        \"article\": null,\n        \"place\": null,\n        \"communityNote\": null,\n        \"isEdited\": false,\n        \"quotedTweet\": null,\n        \"retweetedTweet\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"2056768415604355330\",\n        \"url\": \"https://x.com/coach_Mollring/status/2056768415604355330\",\n        \"text\": \"20 years coaching college football. \\n5 as a head coach. \\n7 years using and then training college coaches on how to recruit at Tudor Collegiate Strategies.\\nI wrote the book on what winning actually looks like inside a program — and I use the same playbook with the families I work with.\\nIf you're a player or parent trying to figure out recruiting, you're not getting generic advice from me. \\nYou're getting the exact framework I taught the coaches who are recruiting you.\\n📘 Book: https://a.co/d/02je4ENm\\n 🎯 Work with me: http://nomoathletics.com\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-05-19T16:06:17.000Z\",\n        \"createdAtUnix\": 1779206777,\n        \"createdAtLabel\": null,\n        \"language\": \"en\",\n        \"conversationId\": \"2056768415604355330\",\n        \"inReplyToStatusId\": null,\n        \"inReplyToUserId\": null,\n        \"inReplyToScreenName\": null,\n        \"quotedStatusId\": null,\n        \"retweetTweetId\": null,\n        \"author\": {\n          \"handle\": \"coach_Mollring\",\n          \"displayName\": \"Grant Mollring\",\n          \"avatarUrl\": \"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2052202930225254406/7_IhQ3Mu_400x400.jpg\",\n          \"profileUrl\": \"https://x.com/coach_Mollring\",\n          \"verified\": false,\n          \"blueVerified\": false,\n          \"platformUserId\": \"3195417666\",\n          \"bio\": \"Former D3 Head Coach & recruiting educator. I know what coaches want — now I help families navigate the process. 🏈 NoMo Athletics | Recruit Accelerator\",\n          \"location\": \"Lincoln, NE\",\n          \"website\": \"http://Nomoathletics.com\",\n          \"bannerUrl\": \"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/3195417666/1778118282/1500x500\",\n          \"accountCreatedAt\": \"2015-05-14T15:48:50.000Z\",\n          \"privateAccount\": false,\n          \"verifiedType\": null,\n          \"affiliateLabel\": null,\n          \"professional\": {\n            \"type\": \"Business\",\n            \"category\": [\n              {\n                \"id\": 800,\n                \"name\": \"Sports, Fitness & Recreation\",\n                \"icon_name\": \"IconBriefcaseStroke\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"restId\": \"2038665470681727379\"\n          },\n          \"metrics\": {\n            \"availableFields\": [\n              \"followers\",\n              \"following\",\n              \"tweets\",\n              \"favourites\",\n              \"listedCount\",\n              \"mediaCount\"\n            ],\n            \"followers\": 4337,\n            \"following\": 3553,\n            \"tweets\": 1822,\n            \"favourites\": 4411,\n            \"listedCount\": 24,\n            \"mediaCount\": 197\n          }\n        },\n        \"metrics\": {\n          \"availableFields\": [\n            \"likes\",\n            \"retweets\",\n            \"replies\",\n            \"quotes\",\n            \"views\",\n            \"bookmarkCount\"\n          ],\n          \"likes\": 6,\n          \"retweets\": 2,\n          \"replies\": 4,\n          \"quotes\": 0,\n          \"views\": 1190,\n          \"bookmarkCount\": 0\n        },\n        \"media\": [],\n        \"expandedUrl\": \"https://a.co/d/02je4ENm\",\n        \"isRetweet\": false,\n        \"isReply\": false,\n        \"isQuote\": false,\n        \"source\": \"Twitter Web App\",\n        \"communityId\": null,\n        \"hasAIGeneratedMedia\": false,\n        \"isPaidPromotion\": false,\n        \"isTranslatable\": false,\n        \"hasBirdwatchNotes\": false,\n        \"possiblySensitive\": false,\n        \"entities\": {\n          \"hashtags\": [],\n          \"userMentions\": [],\n          \"urls\": [\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://a.co/d/02je4ENm\",\n              \"displayUrl\": \"https://a.co/d/02je4ENm\",\n              \"expandedUrl\": \"https://a.co/d/02je4ENm\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"url\": \"http://nomoathletics.com\",\n              \"displayUrl\": \"http://nomoathletics.com\",\n              \"expandedUrl\": \"http://nomoathletics.com\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"symbols\": []\n        },\n        \"card\": {\n          \"type\": \"summary\",\n          \"name\": \"summary_large_image\",\n          \"url\": \"https://t.co/5w9xMCGDyr\",\n          \"title\": \"What Winning Actually Looks LIke\",\n          \"description\": \"Inside this book, you’ll learn: This book is for: What makes this different? If you’re serious about building a program…\",\n          \"domain\": \"www.amazon.com\",\n          \"imageUrl\": \"https://pbs.twimg.com/card_img/2118121137221906432/L2BNYhTc?format=jpg&name=orig\",\n          \"playerUrl\": null,\n          \"appName\": null\n        },\n        \"poll\": null,\n        \"article\": null,\n        \"place\": null,\n        \"communityNote\": null,\n        \"isEdited\": false,\n        \"quotedTweet\": null,\n        \"retweetedTweet\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"2117312457329070575\",\n        \"url\": \"https://x.com/coachdrew94/status/2117312457329070575\",\n        \"text\": \"This morning a father of a '27 player in my program called upset. His son has only heard from D3 and some D2 coaches. He wants D1.\\n\\nHere's what I tried to explain:\\n\\n• His son is a corner outfielder. It's the LAST position college coaches recruit for.\\n• At the D1 level, coaches over-recruit shortstops and move them to the outfield.\\n• Many D1 coaches wait for the transfer portal in December to see what outfielders are available before they commit a roster spot to a high school kid.\\n\\nHe hung up on me.\\n\\nParents, D2 and D3 interest is not a failure. It's real interest from coaches who want your son. Position matters. Timing matters. Know the landscape.\\n\\nCoach Drew\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-11-02T17:46:42.000Z\",\n        \"createdAtUnix\": 1793641602,\n        \"createdAtLabel\": null,\n        \"language\": \"en\",\n        \"conversationId\": \"2117312457329070575\",\n        \"inReplyToStatusId\": null,\n        \"inReplyToUserId\": null,\n        \"inReplyToScreenName\": null,\n        \"quotedStatusId\": null,\n        \"retweetTweetId\": null,\n        \"author\": {\n          \"handle\": \"coachdrew94\",\n          \"displayName\": \"Coach Drew's Recruiting Service - 27 yrs. exp.\",\n          \"avatarUrl\": \"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2117681283660996608/wjkYgCjw_400x400.jpg\",\n          \"profileUrl\": \"https://x.com/coachdrew94\",\n          \"verified\": false,\n          \"blueVerified\": true,\n          \"platformUserId\": \"1667193117597143040\",\n          \"bio\": \"If you're a 27' player with 0 offers, still looking, not ready to give up, I can help you find offers. https://t.co/KBP0klXNsL\",\n          \"location\": \"Serving families nationwide\",\n          \"website\": \"https://coachdrew93.com/\",\n          \"bannerUrl\": \"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/1667193117597143040/1793728987/1500x500\",\n          \"accountCreatedAt\": \"2023-06-09T15:33:27.000Z\",\n          \"privateAccount\": false,\n          \"verifiedType\": null,\n          \"affiliateLabel\": null,\n          \"professional\": null,\n          \"metrics\": {\n            \"availableFields\": [\n              \"followers\",\n              \"following\",\n              \"tweets\",\n              \"favourites\",\n              \"listedCount\",\n              \"mediaCount\"\n            ],\n            \"followers\": 16335,\n            \"following\": 7408,\n            \"tweets\": 4435,\n            \"favourites\": 15,\n            \"listedCount\": 5,\n            \"mediaCount\": 146\n          }\n        },\n        \"metrics\": {\n          \"availableFields\": [\n            \"likes\",\n            \"retweets\",\n            \"replies\",\n            \"quotes\",\n            \"views\",\n            \"bookmarkCount\"\n          ],\n          \"likes\": 729,\n          \"retweets\": 11,\n          \"replies\": 44,\n          \"quotes\": 2,\n          \"views\": 143447,\n          \"bookmarkCount\": 20\n        },\n        \"media\": [],\n        \"expandedUrl\": null,\n        \"isRetweet\": false,\n        \"isReply\": false,\n        \"isQuote\": false,\n        \"source\": null,\n        \"communityId\": null,\n        \"hasAIGeneratedMedia\": false,\n        \"isPaidPromotion\": false,\n        \"isTranslatable\": false,\n        \"hasBirdwatchNotes\": false,\n        \"possiblySensitive\": false,\n        \"entities\": {\n          \"hashtags\": [],\n          \"userMentions\": [],\n          \"urls\": [],\n          \"symbols\": []\n        },\n        \"card\": null,\n        \"poll\": null,\n        \"article\": null,\n        \"place\": null,\n        \"communityNote\": null,\n        \"isEdited\": false,\n        \"quotedTweet\": null,\n        \"retweetedTweet\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"2116116868867952797\",\n        \"url\": \"https://x.com/SFACoachMartin/status/2116116868867952797\",\n        \"text\": \"RECRUITING TALK: STARS, NO STARS & NIL 🏈\\n\\nAs a high school coach, I want players and parents to understand this: recruiting stars can help open doors, but they don’t determine how far you can go.\\n\\nRespect the players who earned those ratings. Many are outstanding athletes who put in serious work. But understand what a star rating represents: a recruiting service’s evaluation and projection at a particular point in a player’s development.\\n\\nIt is not a scholarship, a starting position, a degree or a guaranteed NFL career.\\n\\nAnd being unrated does NOT mean a college coaching staff cannot evaluate you, recruit you or offer you a scholarship.\\n\\nSome players develop later. Some receive less exposure. Some haven’t been evaluated extensively. Others need to improve before they’re ready for the next level. Our job as coaches is to give an honest assessment and help each player build a realistic path.\\n\\nCollege coaches recruit for THEIR roster. Your film, verified measurables, academics, position fit, development and character all matter. A recruiting website doesn’t make their final decision.\\n\\nWant proof that an unrated player can build a professional career? Josh Allen left high school without stars, went through junior college and earned his opportunity at Wyoming. His path proves it is possible—not that it is easy or guaranteed.\\n\\nNow let’s address NIL.\\n\\nThere is no recruiting-star requirement for a legitimate NIL opportunity.\\n\\nNIL means a business compensates you for using your name, image or likeness through activities such as endorsements, promotional content or appearances. Stars may increase visibility, but businesses can also value your audience, community connections, credibility and ability to represent their brand.\\n\\nAn unrated player with an engaged local following and professional habits can offer value to a business. That does not guarantee a deal, and every athlete should have realistic expectations about the money involved.\\n\\nStart building those habits now:\\n\\n• Put quality football on film.\\n• Protect your grades and eligibility.\\n• Make your recruiting information easy to find.\\n• Communicate professionally.\\n• Build authentic community relationships.\\n• Create useful, consistent content.\\n• Follow through when you make a commitment.\\n\\nUnderstand this distinction, too: a scholarship, third-party NIL deal and direct payment from a college are different things. An offer does not automatically include all three.\\n\\nBefore accepting NIL compensation, verify the rules that apply to your school, athletic association and future college. Have agreements reviewed and meet applicable reporting requirements.\\n\\nMy advice: choose a college where you can develop, afford your education and prepare for life. Evaluate the coaching, academics, roster and total financial package.\\n\\nFootball can lead to college, professional opportunities, coaching, business and relationships that last well beyond your playing days. The NFL is one possible outcome—not the only meaningful career.\\n\\nRated players: keep earning it.\\nUnrated players: keep developing and getting evaluated.\\n\\nYour rating can describe where you are today. It cannot finish your story.\\nYou’re welcome.\\n#sfaacadenyfootball \\n#FootballRecruiting #RecruitingEducation #StudentAthlete #NIL #HighSchoolFootball\\n#9091sportsagency\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-30T10:35:51.000Z\",\n        \"createdAtUnix\": 1793356551,\n        \"createdAtLabel\": null,\n        \"language\": \"en\",\n        \"conversationId\": \"2116116868867952797\",\n        \"inReplyToStatusId\": null,\n        \"inReplyToUserId\": null,\n        \"inReplyToScreenName\": null,\n        \"quotedStatusId\": null,\n        \"retweetTweetId\": null,\n        \"author\": {\n          \"handle\": \"SFACoachMartin\",\n          \"displayName\": \"Coach Martin\",\n          \"avatarUrl\": \"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2033611255244533760/3e04yxjb_400x400.jpg\",\n          \"profileUrl\": \"https://x.com/SFACoachMartin\",\n          \"verified\": false,\n          \"blueVerified\": true,\n          \"platformUserId\": \"1594759961170558979\",\n          \"bio\": \"Safeties Coach/Recruiting Coordinator @ SFA \\nhttps://t.co/PI7roM7Kfr\\nhttps://t.co/GUYw4VdQBh\\nFounder:https://t.co/7wuS7qy6Dk\",\n          \"location\": \"Tampa, Florida\",\n          \"website\": \"http://strongfaithathletics.com\",\n          \"bannerUrl\": \"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/1594759961170558979/1673077270/1500x500\",\n          \"accountCreatedAt\": \"2022-11-21T18:30:00.000Z\",\n          \"privateAccount\": false,\n          \"verifiedType\": null,\n          \"affiliateLabel\": null,\n          \"professional\": {\n            \"type\": \"Business\",\n            \"category\": [\n              {\n                \"id\": 800,\n                \"name\": \"Sports, Fitness & Recreation\",\n                \"icon_name\": \"IconBriefcaseStroke\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"restId\": \"1648018533152874496\"\n          },\n          \"metrics\": {\n            \"availableFields\": [\n              \"followers\",\n              \"following\",\n              \"tweets\",\n              \"favourites\",\n              \"listedCount\",\n              \"mediaCount\"\n            ],\n            \"followers\": 3013,\n            \"following\": 5323,\n            \"tweets\": 2303,\n            \"favourites\": 3026,\n            \"listedCount\": 4,\n            \"mediaCount\": 986\n          }\n        },\n        \"metrics\": {\n          \"availableFields\": [\n            \"likes\",\n            \"retweets\",\n            \"replies\",\n            \"quotes\",\n            \"views\",\n            \"bookmarkCount\"\n          ],\n          \"likes\": 21,\n          \"retweets\": 4,\n          \"replies\": 0,\n          \"quotes\": 0,\n          \"views\": 2358,\n          \"bookmarkCount\": 3\n        },\n        \"media\": [],\n        \"expandedUrl\": null,\n        \"isRetweet\": false,\n        \"isReply\": false,\n        \"isQuote\": false,\n        \"source\": null,\n        \"communityId\": null,\n        \"hasAIGeneratedMedia\": false,\n        \"isPaidPromotion\": false,\n        \"isTranslatable\": false,\n        \"hasBirdwatchNotes\": false,\n        \"possiblySensitive\": false,\n        \"entities\": {\n          \"hashtags\": [\n            {\n              \"text\": \"sfaacadenyfootball\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"text\": \"FootballRecruiting\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"text\": \"RecruitingEducation\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"text\": \"StudentAthlete\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"text\": \"NIL\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"text\": \"HighSchoolFootball\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"text\": \"9091sportsagency\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"userMentions\": [],\n          \"urls\": [],\n          \"symbols\": []\n        },\n        \"card\": null,\n        \"poll\": null,\n        \"article\": null,\n        \"place\": null,\n        \"communityNote\": null,\n        \"isEdited\": false,\n        \"quotedTweet\": null,\n        \"retweetedTweet\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"2118733820728082922\",\n        \"url\": \"https://x.com/coachdrew94/status/2118733820728082922\",\n        \"text\": \"Hey! Quick favor.\\n\\nDo you know a teammate or friend who can play in college but is still looking, or is ready to give up because he has no offers?\\n\\nI'd love to help him. Phase 2 is when most families stop, and it's when I find players their opportunities.\\n\\nHave him or his parents go to my site and complete the evaluation and scholarship application:\\nhttps://coachdrew93.com/\\n\\nThanks for thinking of me. It means a lot.\\n\\nCoach Drew\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-11-06T15:54:41.000Z\",\n        \"createdAtUnix\": 1793980481,\n        \"createdAtLabel\": null,\n        \"language\": \"en\",\n        \"conversationId\": \"2118733820728082922\",\n        \"inReplyToStatusId\": null,\n        \"inReplyToUserId\": null,\n        \"inReplyToScreenName\": null,\n        \"quotedStatusId\": null,\n        \"retweetTweetId\": null,\n        \"author\": {\n          \"handle\": \"coachdrew94\",\n          \"displayName\": \"Coach Drew's Recruiting Service - 27 yrs. exp.\",\n          \"avatarUrl\": \"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2117681283660996608/wjkYgCjw_400x400.jpg\",\n          \"profileUrl\": \"https://x.com/coachdrew94\",\n          \"verified\": false,\n          \"blueVerified\": true,\n          \"platformUserId\": \"1667193117597143040\",\n          \"bio\": \"If you're a 27' player with 0 offers, still looking, not ready to give up, I can help you find offers. https://t.co/KBP0klXNsL\",\n          \"location\": \"Serving families nationwide\",\n          \"website\": \"https://coachdrew93.com/\",\n          \"bannerUrl\": \"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/1667193117597143040/1793728987/1500x500\",\n          \"accountCreatedAt\": \"2023-06-09T15:33:27.000Z\",\n          \"privateAccount\": false,\n          \"verifiedType\": null,\n          \"affiliateLabel\": null,\n          \"professional\": null,\n          \"metrics\": {\n            \"availableFields\": [\n              \"followers\",\n              \"following\",\n              \"tweets\",\n              \"favourites\",\n              \"listedCount\",\n              \"mediaCount\"\n            ],\n            \"followers\": 16335,\n            \"following\": 7408,\n            \"tweets\": 4435,\n            \"favourites\": 15,\n            \"listedCount\": 5,\n            \"mediaCount\": 146\n          }\n        },\n        \"metrics\": {\n          \"availableFields\": [\n            \"likes\",\n            \"retweets\",\n            \"replies\",\n            \"quotes\",\n            \"views\",\n            \"bookmarkCount\"\n          ],\n          \"likes\": 0,\n          \"retweets\": 0,\n          \"replies\": 0,\n          \"quotes\": 0,\n          \"views\": 98,\n          \"bookmarkCount\": 0\n        },\n        \"media\": [],\n        \"expandedUrl\": \"https://coachdrew93.com/\",\n        \"isRetweet\": false,\n        \"isReply\": false,\n        \"isQuote\": false,\n        \"source\": null,\n        \"communityId\": null,\n        \"hasAIGeneratedMedia\": false,\n        \"isPaidPromotion\": false,\n        \"isTranslatable\": false,\n        \"hasBirdwatchNotes\": false,\n        \"possiblySensitive\": false,\n        \"entities\": {\n          \"hashtags\": [],\n          \"userMentions\": [],\n          \"urls\": [\n            {\n              \"url\": \"https://coachdrew93.com/\",\n              \"displayUrl\": \"https://coachdrew93.com/\",\n              \"expandedUrl\": \"https://coachdrew93.com/\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"symbols\": []\n        },\n        \"card\": {\n          \"type\": \"summary\",\n          \"name\": \"summary\",\n          \"url\": \"https://t.co/xxqtBnTfbp\",\n          \"title\": \"Coach Drew | College Recruiting · 27 Years · 4,413+ Players Placed\",\n          \"description\": \"Coach Drew Sikorski: 27+ years working with college coaches and 4,413+ players placed at D1, D2, D3, NAIA and JUCO. CDRI Evaluation $79.95, Phase 2 recruiting and the Private Program.\",\n          \"domain\": \"coachdrew93.com\",\n          \"imageUrl\": null,\n          \"playerUrl\": null,\n          \"appName\": null\n        },\n        \"poll\": null,\n        \"article\": null,\n        \"place\": null,\n        \"communityNote\": null,\n        \"isEdited\": false,\n        \"quotedTweet\": null,\n        \"retweetedTweet\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"2118410522093613557\",\n        \"url\": \"https://x.com/The_CAAdvantage/status/2118410522093613557\",\n        \"text\": \"One of the most frustrating parts of the recruiting process is when you reach out to college coaches and hear absolutely NOTHING back. 👎🏼\\n\\nYou start wondering \\\"What am I doing wrong?!\\\" 😩\\n\\nThe reality is that a lack of responses from college coaches doesn’t necessarily mean you/your athlete can’t play in college, but it DOES mean you need to take a closer look at your recruiting strategy. 🔍\\n\\nCollege coaches receive hundreds of emails, so they filter through prospects quickly. If they can’t evaluate you quickly, they may move on....\\n\\nSo what can you do about it? 👇\\n\\n1️⃣ Evaluate the schools you’re contacting. If you are reaching out to programs above your ability level, you won’t receive many responses.\\n\\n2️⃣ Second, evaluate your message. Your emails should make key information easily accessible, including graduation year, key metrics/stats, video links, and academic information.\\n\\n3️⃣ Third, follow up with a purpose. Send meaningful updates when you improves, achieve something significant, or have new video available.\\n\\nBottom Line 👉 Don’t interpret silence as a final verdict on your athlete’s ability, but don’t ignore it either. If you’re contacting dozens of coaches and getting very few responses, something probably needs to change.\\n\\nAnd if your family is frustrated by a lack of communication from college coaches and you're unsure what to do differently, message us and ask to schedule a free recruiting consultation. 💪\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-11-05T18:30:01.000Z\",\n        \"createdAtUnix\": 1793903401,\n        \"createdAtLabel\": null,\n        \"language\": \"en\",\n        \"conversationId\": \"2118410522093613557\",\n        \"inReplyToStatusId\": null,\n        \"inReplyToUserId\": null,\n        \"inReplyToScreenName\": null,\n        \"quotedStatusId\": null,\n        \"retweetTweetId\": null,\n        \"author\": {\n          \"handle\": \"The_CAAdvantage\",\n          \"displayName\": \"College Athlete Advantage\",\n          \"avatarUrl\": \"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1820939234616004608/7zXRV1lz_400x400.jpg\",\n          \"profileUrl\": \"https://x.com/The_CAAdvantage\",\n          \"verified\": false,\n          \"blueVerified\": true,\n          \"platformUserId\": \"1023658809565179906\",\n          \"bio\": \"A group of former college coaches and players that help advise student athletes in today's baseball recruiting world.\",\n          \"location\": \"Tempe, AZ\",\n          \"website\": \"http://collegeathleteadvantage.com\",\n          \"bannerUrl\": \"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/1023658809565179906/1769970062/1500x500\",\n          \"accountCreatedAt\": \"2018-07-29T19:57:33.000Z\",\n          \"privateAccount\": false,\n          \"verifiedType\": null,\n          \"affiliateLabel\": null,\n          \"professional\": {\n            \"type\": \"Business\",\n            \"category\": [\n              {\n                \"id\": 800,\n                \"name\": \"Sports, Fitness & Recreation\",\n                \"icon_name\": \"IconBriefcaseStroke\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"restId\": \"1470022764295692288\"\n          },\n          \"metrics\": {\n            \"availableFields\": [\n              \"followers\",\n              \"following\",\n              \"tweets\",\n              \"favourites\",\n              \"listedCount\",\n              \"mediaCount\"\n            ],\n            \"followers\": 9348,\n            \"following\": 4052,\n            \"tweets\": 6558,\n            \"favourites\": 4537,\n            \"listedCount\": 8,\n            \"mediaCount\": 4265\n          }\n        },\n        \"metrics\": {\n          \"availableFields\": [\n            \"likes\",\n            \"retweets\",\n            \"replies\",\n            \"quotes\",\n            \"views\",\n            \"bookmarkCount\"\n          ],\n          \"likes\": 0,\n          \"retweets\": 0,\n          \"replies\": 0,\n          \"quotes\": 0,\n          \"views\": 162,\n          \"bookmarkCount\": 0\n        },\n        \"media\": [\n          {\n            \"url\": \"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HWYbJGYXwAEUyXn.jpg\",\n            \"type\": \"photo\",\n            \"width\": 1080,\n            \"height\": 1080,\n            \"id\": \"2118410517870002177\",\n            \"altText\": null\n          }\n        ],\n        \"expandedUrl\": null,\n        \"isRetweet\": false,\n        \"isReply\": false,\n        \"isQuote\": false,\n        \"source\": null,\n        \"communityId\": null,\n        \"hasAIGeneratedMedia\": false,\n        \"isPaidPromotion\": false,\n        \"isTranslatable\": false,\n        \"hasBirdwatchNotes\": false,\n        \"possiblySensitive\": false,\n        \"entities\": {\n          \"hashtags\": [],\n          \"userMentions\": [],\n          \"urls\": [],\n          \"symbols\": []\n        },\n        \"card\": null,\n        \"poll\": null,\n        \"article\": null,\n        \"place\": null,\n        \"communityNote\": null,\n        \"isEdited\": false,\n        \"quotedTweet\": null,\n        \"retweetedTweet\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"2083985956969804099\",\n        \"url\": \"https://x.com/nlevelsports/status/2083985956969804099\",\n        \"text\": \"http://x.com/i/article/2083985175365468160\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-02T18:39:05.000Z\",\n        \"createdAtUnix\": 1785695945,\n        \"createdAtLabel\": null,\n        \"language\": \"zxx\",\n        \"conversationId\": \"2083985956969804099\",\n        \"inReplyToStatusId\": null,\n        \"inReplyToUserId\": null,\n        \"inReplyToScreenName\": null,\n        \"quotedStatusId\": null,\n        \"retweetTweetId\": null,\n        \"author\": {\n          \"handle\": \"nlevelsports\",\n          \"displayName\": \"Next Level Sports\",\n          \"avatarUrl\": \"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1586746762575986688/1kVB9g4o_400x400.jpg\",\n          \"profileUrl\": \"https://x.com/nlevelsports\",\n          \"verified\": false,\n          \"blueVerified\": true,\n          \"platformUserId\": \"1586746704895922176\",\n          \"bio\": \"Helping high school athletes get recruited to college 🏈🏀⚾\\nPro Recruiting Profiles • Highlight Exposure • Coach Connections\\nTag us in your highlights for a RT\",\n          \"location\": null,\n          \"website\": \"http://nlevelsports.net\",\n          \"bannerUrl\": \"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/1586746704895922176/1667161095/1500x500\",\n          \"accountCreatedAt\": \"2022-10-30T15:47:54.000Z\",\n          \"privateAccount\": false,\n          \"verifiedType\": null,\n          \"affiliateLabel\": null,\n          \"professional\": {\n            \"type\": \"Business\",\n            \"category\": [\n              {\n                \"id\": 800,\n                \"name\": \"Sports, Fitness & Recreation\",\n                \"icon_name\": \"IconBriefcaseStroke\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"restId\": \"1586814446139281411\"\n          },\n          \"metrics\": {\n            \"availableFields\": [\n              \"followers\",\n              \"following\",\n              \"tweets\",\n              \"favourites\",\n              \"listedCount\",\n              \"mediaCount\"\n            ],\n            \"followers\": 11286,\n            \"following\": 850,\n            \"tweets\": 7193,\n            \"favourites\": 97853,\n            \"listedCount\": 5,\n            \"mediaCount\": 1140\n          }\n        },\n        \"metrics\": {\n          \"availableFields\": [\n            \"likes\",\n            \"retweets\",\n            \"replies\",\n            \"quotes\",\n            \"views\",\n            \"bookmarkCount\"\n          ],\n          \"likes\": 2,\n          \"retweets\": 0,\n          \"replies\": 0,\n          \"quotes\": 1,\n          \"views\": 970,\n          \"bookmarkCount\": 0\n        },\n        \"media\": [],\n        \"expandedUrl\": \"http://x.com/i/article/2083985175365468160\",\n        \"isRetweet\": false,\n        \"isReply\": false,\n        \"isQuote\": false,\n        \"source\": null,\n        \"communityId\": null,\n        \"hasAIGeneratedMedia\": false,\n        \"isPaidPromotion\": false,\n        \"isTranslatable\": false,\n        \"hasBirdwatchNotes\": false,\n        \"possiblySensitive\": false,\n        \"entities\": {\n          \"hashtags\": [],\n          \"userMentions\": [],\n          \"urls\": [\n            {\n              \"url\": \"http://x.com/i/article/2083985175365468160\",\n              \"displayUrl\": \"http://x.com/i/article/2083985175365468160\",\n              \"expandedUrl\": \"http://x.com/i/article/2083985175365468160\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"symbols\": []\n        },\n        \"card\": null,\n        \"poll\": null,\n        \"article\": {\n          \"title\": \"The Coach Email Formula: How to Write a Message That Gets Read\",\n          \"previewText\": \"College coaches receive dozens (sometimes hundreds) of emails every week from athletes and parents. Most of them get deleted, skimmed, or ignored.\\nThe ones that get read follow a clear pattern.\\nHere’s\",\n          \"id\": \"2083985175365468160\",\n          \"text\": null,\n          \"coverImageUrl\": \"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HOvN658WQAA7Sfu.jpg\"\n        },\n        \"place\": null,\n        \"communityNote\": null,\n        \"isEdited\": false,\n        \"quotedTweet\": null,\n        \"retweetedTweet\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"people\": [],\n    \"page\": {\n      \"nextCursor\": \"\",\n      \"hasMore\": true\n    }\n  },\n  \"meta\": {\n    \"requestId\": \"req_4d365926-e473-4057-a88a-9fb85763f2eb\",\n    \"creditsCharged\": 1,\n    \"version\": \"v1\"\n  }\n}"},{"type":"text","text":"{\"conversation_id\":\"01a1b1a6-e4af-70fc-ba65-efaec43e70a9\"}"}],"structuredContent":{"data":{"tweets":[{"id":"2064370062811697629","url":"https://x.com/CoachCarm/status/2064370062811697629","text":"Tip for parents on college visits. One thing coaches and leaders of organizations look for when recruiting high potential individuals is their ability to communicate. \n\nOne red flag 🚩 to a coach and his staff is a parent or family member who often speaks for their son or daughter. Let them answer. \n#Recruit #Advice #RedFlags #Wisdom #Recruiting #NCAA","createdAt":"2026-06-09T15:32:31.000Z","createdAtUnix":1781019151,"createdAtLabel":null,"language":"en","conversationId":"2064370062811697629","inReplyToStatusId":null,"inReplyToUserId":null,"inReplyToScreenName":null,"quotedStatusId":null,"retweetTweetId":null,"author":{"handle":"CoachCarm","displayName":"Carmen Maciariello","avatarUrl":"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1898140983155466242/q-i5eanM_400x400.jpg","profileUrl":"https://x.com/CoachCarm","verified":false,"blueVerified":false,"platformUserId":"25149160","bio":"Army Basketball Assistant Coach","location":"West Point, NY","website":"https://goarmywestpoint.com","bannerUrl":"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/25149160/1792165825/1500x500","accountCreatedAt":"2009-03-18T20:39:10.000Z","privateAccount":false,"verifiedType":null,"affiliateLabel":null,"professional":null,"metrics":{"availableFields":["followers","following","tweets","favourites","listedCount","mediaCount"],"followers":15301,"following":3713,"tweets":8416,"favourites":45638,"listedCount":69,"mediaCount":876}},"metrics":{"availableFields":["likes","retweets","replies","quotes","views","bookmarkCount"],"likes":24,"retweets":9,"replies":0,"quotes":3,"views":6058,"bookmarkCount":5},"media":[],"expandedUrl":null,"isRetweet":false,"isReply":false,"isQuote":false,"source":null,"communityId":null,"hasAIGeneratedMedia":false,"isPaidPromotion":false,"isTranslatable":false,"hasBirdwatchNotes":false,"possiblySensitive":false,"entities":{"hashtags":[{"text":"Recruit"},{"text":"Advice"},{"text":"RedFlags"},{"text":"Wisdom"},{"text":"Recruiting"},{"text":"NCAA"}],"userMentions":[],"urls":[],"symbols":[]},"card":null,"poll":null,"article":null,"place":null,"communityNote":null,"isEdited":false,"quotedTweet":null,"retweetedTweet":null},{"id":"2020525684502778103","url":"https://x.com/playgolfcollege/status/2020525684502778103","text":"Everyone in junior golf has an opinion about college recruiting. The swing coach. The club pro. The parent whose kid committed last year. The recruiting service that charges thousands for a templated email blast.\n\nMost of them mean well. But meaning well and knowing what you're talking about are two very different things.\n\nHere's a question worth asking before you take anyone's advice on college golf recruiting: Have they ever actually coached in college? Do they have real relationships with the coaches your child is trying to play for?\n\nBecause if they haven't, they're guessing. And guessing with your child's future is expensive.\n\n𝗧𝗵𝗲 𝗚𝗮𝗽 𝗕𝗲𝘁𝘄𝗲𝗲𝗻 𝗜𝗻𝘁𝗲𝗻𝘁𝗶𝗼𝗻 𝗮𝗻𝗱 𝗘𝘅𝗽𝗲𝗿𝗶𝗲𝗻𝗰𝗲\n\nA lot of people can tell you how recruiting is supposed to work. They've read about it. They've heard stories. Maybe they went through it once with their own child.\n\nBut there's a difference between going through recruiting as a family and understanding recruiting from the coach's side of the table. Knowing what coaches are actually evaluating. Knowing why certain players get offers and others don't despite similar scores. Knowing the internal dynamics of roster management, scholarship allocation, and how coaches talk about recruits behind closed doors.\n\nThat only comes from being in the room. I've been in the room.\n\n𝗥𝗲𝗹𝗮𝘁𝗶𝗼𝗻𝘀𝗵𝗶𝗽𝘀 𝗠𝗮𝘁𝘁𝗲𝗿 𝗠𝗼𝗿𝗲 𝗧𝗵𝗮𝗻 𝗣𝗲𝗼𝗽𝗹𝗲 𝗥𝗲𝗮𝗹𝗶𝘇𝗲\n\nHere's something most families never think about. When a college coach gets a call or an email from someone recommending a player, the first thing they ask themselves is: Do I trust this person? Do they understand what I need on my roster? Have they ever sent me a player who wasn't what they said he was?\n\nI know these coaches personally. Not from cold emails or LinkedIn connections. From years of working alongside them, competing against them, and sending them players who showed up ready. When I call a college coach about one of my players, they take the call. They trust my evaluation because they know I understand what they're looking for. I've been in their shoes. I know what it takes to build a roster, manage a team, and develop players at that level.\n\nThat trust isn't something you can fake or buy. It's earned over decades. And it matters enormously in recruiting, because a personal recommendation from someone a coach respects carries more weight than any highlight reel or ranking.\n\n𝗪𝗵𝗮𝘁 𝗜'𝘃𝗲 𝗦𝗲𝗲𝗻 𝗧𝗵𝗮𝘁 𝗠𝗼𝘀𝘁 𝗣𝗲𝗼𝗽𝗹𝗲 𝗛𝗮𝘃𝗲𝗻'𝘁\n\nI coached at Duke and Ohio State. I was part of NCAA championship teams. I know what a college coach sees when they watch a junior golfer at a tournament, and it's not what most families think. Coaches are watching how you handle a triple bogey. They're watching whether you're engaged with your playing partners or buried in your phone. They're watching how you interact with your parents between rounds. They're watching everything.\n\nI know this because I was the one watching.\n\nOver 16 years of running Play Golf In College, I've helped more than 165 players earn spots on college rosters. Nineteen individual state champions. The number one high school team in the country. A 95% success rate. And I went through the entire process personally with my own three kids who all played Division I golf.\n\nThose aren't just numbers. They're relationships. Every one of those placements strengthened my connection with the coaches at those programs. Every player who showed up prepared and ready reinforced the trust that makes the next phone call matter.","createdAt":"2026-02-08T15:50:37.000Z","createdAtUnix":1770565837,"createdAtLabel":null,"language":"en","conversationId":"2020525684502778103","inReplyToStatusId":null,"inReplyToUserId":null,"inReplyToScreenName":null,"quotedStatusId":null,"retweetTweetId":null,"author":{"handle":"playgolfcollege","displayName":"Brad Sparling","avatarUrl":"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1075401267931942913/_bOL0Bem_400x400.jpg","profileUrl":"https://x.com/playgolfcollege","verified":false,"blueVerified":true,"platformUserId":"263825974","bio":"Development and Recruiting. Former Duke coach. 165+ players placed in college. Free weekly letter for golf parents. https://t.co/9lqr2UAN7z","location":"Dublin, Ohio","website":"http://www.playgolfincollege.com","bannerUrl":"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/263825974/1455812883/1500x500","accountCreatedAt":"2011-03-10T20:29:01.000Z","privateAccount":false,"verifiedType":null,"affiliateLabel":null,"professional":null,"metrics":{"availableFields":["followers","following","tweets","favourites","listedCount","mediaCount"],"followers":1636,"following":874,"tweets":6541,"favourites":12313,"listedCount":10,"mediaCount":617}},"metrics":{"availableFields":["likes","retweets","replies","quotes","views","bookmarkCount"],"likes":1,"retweets":0,"replies":1,"quotes":0,"views":266,"bookmarkCount":3},"media":[],"expandedUrl":null,"isRetweet":false,"isReply":false,"isQuote":false,"source":"Twitter for iPhone","communityId":null,"hasAIGeneratedMedia":false,"isPaidPromotion":false,"isTranslatable":false,"hasBirdwatchNotes":false,"possiblySensitive":false,"entities":{"hashtags":[],"userMentions":[],"urls":[],"symbols":[]},"card":null,"poll":null,"article":null,"place":null,"communityNote":null,"isEdited":false,"quotedTweet":null,"retweetedTweet":null},{"id":"2117299714349752685","url":"https://x.com/CoachPynnCAA/status/2117299714349752685","text":"After working exclusively in the college baseball recruiting space for the last 10 years, I've noticed a consistent pattern:\n\nThe players who tend to have the most success in the recruiting process often have parents who share the following traits 👇\n\nThat old saying, \"The apple doesn't fall far from the tree,\" holds a lot of truth.\n\nDid I miss anything? Do you recognize any of these traits in yourself? Are there areas you're working on?\n\nWould love to hear your thoughts!\n\n@The_CAAdvantage @CoachRodey\n#BaseballRecruiting #CollegeBaseball","createdAt":"2026-11-02T16:56:04.000Z","createdAtUnix":1793638564,"createdAtLabel":null,"language":"en","conversationId":"2117299714349752685","inReplyToStatusId":null,"inReplyToUserId":null,"inReplyToScreenName":null,"quotedStatusId":null,"retweetTweetId":null,"author":{"handle":"CoachPynnCAA","displayName":"Shawn Pynn (CAA)","avatarUrl":"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/776888025120903168/qleNYCuF_400x400.jpg","profileUrl":"https://x.com/CoachPynnCAA","verified":false,"blueVerified":true,"platformUserId":"776879666405707776","bio":"Recruiting Coach @ College Athlete Advantage\n12 years as a college/pro coach and 10 more years working with 2500+ athletes. Looking for guidance? My DM is open!","location":null,"website":"http://collegeathleteadvantage.com","bannerUrl":"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/776879666405707776/1792720127/1500x500","accountCreatedAt":"2016-09-16T20:25:21.000Z","privateAccount":false,"verifiedType":null,"affiliateLabel":null,"professional":null,"metrics":{"availableFields":["followers","following","tweets","favourites","listedCount","mediaCount"],"followers":2626,"following":124,"tweets":793,"favourites":3085,"listedCount":8,"mediaCount":18}},"metrics":{"availableFields":["likes","retweets","replies","quotes","views","bookmarkCount"],"likes":22,"retweets":4,"replies":3,"quotes":0,"views":8001,"bookmarkCount":5},"media":[{"url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HWInVSXWsAAQ_Am.jpg","type":"photo","width":1254,"height":1254,"id":"2117298021478084608","altText":null}],"expandedUrl":null,"isRetweet":false,"isReply":false,"isQuote":false,"source":null,"communityId":null,"hasAIGeneratedMedia":true,"isPaidPromotion":false,"isTranslatable":false,"hasBirdwatchNotes":false,"possiblySensitive":false,"entities":{"hashtags":[{"text":"BaseballRecruiting"},{"text":"CollegeBaseball"}],"userMentions":[{"handle":"The_CAAdvantage","displayName":"College Athlete Advantage","platformUserId":"1023658809565179906"},{"handle":"CoachRodey","displayName":"Rob Rodebaugh CAA","platformUserId":"1833141821196644352"}],"urls":[],"symbols":[]},"card":null,"poll":null,"article":null,"place":null,"communityNote":null,"isEdited":false,"quotedTweet":null,"retweetedTweet":null},{"id":"1845878659606876384","url":"https://x.com/Chris_M_Cousins/status/1845878659606876384","text":"An Open Letter to Parents/Players looking to play in College after high school\n\nFor some time I've wanted to write something to everyone in this group, who are going through, or about to start, the College Soccer recruiting process for themselves or their child.\n\nThis group is mostly parents, and I totally understand why. If my child wanted to play in College (which I'm sure they will in the future - the oldest is 11), I'd want to understand as much about what's ahead as possible and navigate the journey as efficiently as possible.\n\nBut the problem is, I just don't think people are.\n\nI think watching some of the questions coming in, the comments on this group and others, it just comes across as a bit of a minefield. Which honestly, it is.\n\nI'm going to try help you all, and I'm going to say this as honest as I can, and there is ZERO intent to hurt any feelings. As a parent, I just want people to move forward in this journey as stress free as possible.\n\nSo lets get started...\n\nFirstly, and this comment is probably aimed at 90% of you in this group.\n\nIf you are having to find out how to go through the college soccer recruitment process, this honestly means, your kid is not in the top 25-30% of players available out there.\n\nThose players are typically organically recruited.\n\nYou know, the best players, at the best levels. The players who are just known, and can almost sit back and wait for coaches to come to them. Coaches know of all the top players in the country from Sophomore/Junior year (if not earlier).\n\nThe best teams, go after the best players. Even some of the not great teams do, and try to shoot their shot.\n\nThis may sound obvious, but why am I telling you this.\n\nQuite simply, because I see people talking about schools that will honestly be never interested in them as a freshman.\n\nPeople say they are being talked to by big schools, but you honestly know if you are being recruited, and most of the time you are just being invited to a camp.\n\nNow, do players from average levels get recruited by top schools. Yes, but honestly, its hardly ever.\n\nImagine you are a coach. A player plays for a top professional academy, or national team level. Their view on that player will be high from the start as scouting has been done by others because they are playing at the level they are. They are less of a risk, because many people have 'validated' that player.\n\nNow imagine you are playing for a random club, in a random league. Does that mean you are a bad player, no! But that means (according to others) you aren't top level. If you were, you'd know. You'd be invited to national team camps, pro clubs across the world, etc.\n\nThese are the sorts of players who should just not waste their time (in my opinion) almost begging teams to take them.\n\nThe problem is, people are asking themselves: What do you do if you want to study at a top school but aren't good enough to be recruited?\nHonestly, you've got two choices:\n1) Go to that school, play Club Soccer, and enjoy your dream school. At best, you may make a name for the club team and they may recruit you to the main varsity team.\n2) Take a gamble, and just go into the college soccer system, play and hope that you are going to do well enough to end up at a top team.\n\nThe problem we have these days is, College Soccer, has completely changed over the last 5-10 years. There are so many players available domestically and internationally available. There is always someone better than your child.\n\nBefore I say this harsh reality, you've got to understand one thing. The vast majority of coaches HAVE to win to keep their job. Long gone are the days of just having a coach, coaching away, with zero pressure for results.\nSo the harsh reality is, coaches want players who will help them win.\n\nBeing in this industry for a LONG time, I've seen recruiting go from, \"Yea Chris we'll take him/her, and we'll work on developing him/her\". So now, where MANY coaches just ask for 'immediate impact players'.\n\nAnd they can ask that. Because there's so many of those type of players available worldwide.\n\nI'm not going to get into the whole, \"there's too many internationals\" thing, as there's arguments for both sides, and honestly its out of our control. This post is designed to give you the knowledge and tools to help your child (or yourself) navigate the college soccer recruitment process effectively.\n\nSo what should we do I can hear you asking...\n\nFirst things first, get some honest neutral advice on what level you are at. Its tough to find that these days because even people who think they know college (and may have been involved years ago), don't know the current landscape.\n\nHowever, there's usually always someone who you know who could give you that advice. Usually most people have coach at their club who also works in college or has recently.\n\nWhoever it is, ask them to be HONEST!!! No sugar coating. It may hurt your feelings, but it'll save you so much time.\n\nI meant this with as much empathy as possible, if you are having to ask this question, you are not a top recruit available to coaches.\n\nOnce you've got that information, now you can figure out a plan.\n\nBefore I give you that plan, here is typically what all the levels are asking for these days from High School aged players:\nD1 - TOP MLS Next, or players from top professional clubs around the world.\nD2 (top-mid) - Rarely ask about domestic kids because they can't get the top ones, so they ask for the top professional club players who are getting released.\nD2 (low end) - Ask for decent GPA players with a good budget.\nD3 - They want top GPA's, high budgets.\nNAIA - Rarely ask about domestic kids because they can't get the top ones, so they ask for the top professional club players who are getting released.\nJunior College - They want the top players who aren't eligible to go to the NCAA or NAIA. They also want decent budget kids who can fill up their rosters and hopefully make an impact.\n\nI know people will read these and find/know expections. But this is a general statement for each. I can't possibly write 1500 different example requests for each school :)\n\nNext up athletic scholarships...\n\nAll high school aged players are UNPROVEN college players. They are a gamble. So many coaches, with the amount of players available worldwide and transfers in college, don't need to take gambles. So big athletic scholarships are honestly rare at 4-Year schools from Year 1.\n\nImagine it like any job: you go into the role, do well, then you can ask for a pay rise. Thats typically how soccer scholarships work these days.\n\nThe high athletic scholarships for players who are typically reading this are given at the Junior College level. But even then, there's not many who have that ability to do so.\n\nSo look at this as a situation where you are planning long term. Its not where you start its where you finish.\n\nI always use that phrase, because I truly believe more people need to look at this journey like that.\n\nEarlier today I was reviewing some past clients who were domestic players who ONLY wanted to go D1. Without getting into details, most if not all, played zero to minimal minutes year 1 and 2. Then they wanted to transfer.\n\nI also saw an international player from the middle east, who had the same mindset, so he went to an average D1, didn't play, transferred after year 2 to a D3, and hardly played, and then just quit.\n\nALL of the players who I checked out, just wouldn't listen to what we advised.\n\nWe all know soccer is about opinions, so ours isn't definitive. We get it wrong. But we make informed advice when helping our clients.\n\nAnyway back to you.\n\nSo what should you do...\n\nBy this point you've asked someone neutral, who knows the system, what levels you are suitable for.\n\nNow you have such powerful information in your hands (if its correct obviously). You can start narrowing down your search.\n\nYou should now start looking at schools in those divisions (or maybe its just one), and you need to get on their radar.\n\nAs I said before, these divisions are likely NOT to be D1, so you'll get better responses back when emailing coaches.\n\nEmailing for me is old fashioned, but honestly, you have no other way to get to the coaches. They get 100's of emails a week. So prepare to be ignored, but if they like the look of you, they'll typically reply.\n\nSo this is what you should do.\n\nMake the subject to the point, but make you stand out (if you can).\n\nIf you were a coach, which email subject line would catch your eye more:\n\n1) Striker - ECNL level - 3.5 GPA - High Budget - Available Fall 2025\n2) Striker for Fall 2025\n\nThe answer is 1. Thats because it already tells a story and gives vital info. If a coach NEEDS high budget players, it'll save him time, and save you time too. It'll stop wasteful communication if its never going to work.\n\nSome coaches may make offers reviewing videos. But many will invite you to their camps, or come watch you playing in events.\n\nAt least by this point, you know who's interested, then you can start doing research. That may mean just jumping google maps, having a street-view 'drive' around campus, seeing if its for you. Or even going to visit the school. Or asking people who know about it.\n\nThis should help narrow down.\n\nOnce you are at this point, the ball is in your court. You should be speaking with coaches, have offers on the table, and then you've got to make the right decision for you and your family.\n\nOh, highlight videos...\n\nThis is easy. You need 3 types of videos in your artillery.\n\n1) A 2-3 highlight video. Leave out the music. Make the first minute a compilation of all your best attributes.\n2) 2 x Full Games where you feel comfortable a coach watching you\n3) A video from your best full 90 minute game, and just clip ALL your touches, good and bad.\n\nNo one needs to look perfect. If you were you'd be at Real Madrid. Just sell you, and if someone likes that, thats what you want.\n\nWe are getting to the end.\n\nI hope this has helped at least one of you have a clear picture about things, and there's just a couple more things that are important to add to that foundation of knowledge.\n\n1) New NCAA rules\nThey are looking to bring in rules to limit rosters. This will make it tougher to get to the D1 level, but there's a trickle down affect where players who may have been D1 level roster players, are no longer, so they go to D2, and so on. Just be open minded that there's more people wanting to play College Soccer than there are roster spaces.\n\n2) Social Media\nI'm honestly not a fan of when people create a special Twitter profile, just for recruiting. I personally get followed by about 5 a day. They all look the same. It's a little bit like the email situation. Unless there's something catchy in their bio, then I don't follow back. In regards to social media in general, just be careful what you put on. Coaches search for people online to see what sort of character they have. People share too much. I've seen too many people lose scholarships due to their social media posts.\n\n3) Timeline\nThis is a tough one, but it really coincides with what I've said from the start. If you are very good, you'll organically be recruited. But the vast majority in the 'normal' category, you need to get the ball rolling as a Sophomore (girls), and Junior (boys). Most mens teams don't really recruit the majority of their players until after their season is finished in the year they are looking to bring you in. For girls, they are more open to get girls on their radar.\n\n4) Watch College Games\nThis is short and sweet, the vast majority of people who want to play college soccer have NEVER watched a college game. Get out to your local school, whatever the level, and build that knowledge base of understanding the levels. The amount of girls we've told to go watch a D1 game and they've gone \"WOW - I wasn't expecting them to be so big, athletic, fast\". You'll be surprised at teams across all levels.\n\nTo conclude, and I really hope people have taken this in an empathetic way. I just want to help people. I HATE seeing people wasting time. For me it's not a delusion of the player/parent, it's purely an educational thing\n\nCollege Soccer is different to all the other sports. There are good teams and bad teams in ALL divisions. This isn't basketball and football (American) where the best is D1 without doubt. This is the global game, so coaches can recruit from all corners. Hence why the levels are getting better and better.\n\nAnyway, that was a long letter. If you've got to the end, well done, and hopefully it gives you a clearer idea on your goals!\n\nFor anyone who doesn't know who I am, I founded @SRUSA_Official, the World's Leading #CollegeSoccer Recruiting Agency, so feel free to drop me an email if you are struggling with anything. Always happy to help when I've got a spare 2 minutes. My email is chris@sportsrecruitingusa.com\n\nThanks guys! Have a good one.","createdAt":"2024-10-14T17:25:41.000Z","createdAtUnix":1728926741,"createdAtLabel":null,"language":"en","conversationId":"1845878659606876384","inReplyToStatusId":null,"inReplyToUserId":null,"inReplyToScreenName":null,"quotedStatusId":null,"retweetTweetId":null,"author":{"handle":"Chris_M_Cousins","displayName":"Chris Cousins | 🇺🇸 College Soccer Recruiting","avatarUrl":"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2100570261816823809/ibgbsRDB_400x400.jpg","profileUrl":"https://x.com/Chris_M_Cousins","verified":false,"blueVerified":true,"platformUserId":"557085581","bio":"Founder of 🇺🇸 #CollegeSoccer Recruiting Agency @SRUSA_Official/ Parkland College 🇺🇸 and Leeds Beckett Uni 🇬🇧 Alum / #bcafc fan / All my own views","location":"Dubai 🇦🇪/Sotogrande 🇪🇸","website":"http://www.sportsrecruitingusa.com","bannerUrl":"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/557085581/1635431380/1500x500","accountCreatedAt":"2012-04-18T18:01:27.000Z","privateAccount":false,"verifiedType":null,"affiliateLabel":null,"professional":{"type":"Creator","category":[{"id":800,"name":"Sports, Fitness & Recreation","icon_name":"IconBriefcaseStroke"}],"restId":"1768386910144049587"},"metrics":{"availableFields":["followers","following","tweets","favourites","listedCount","mediaCount"],"followers":6423,"following":2550,"tweets":10157,"favourites":6359,"listedCount":22,"mediaCount":934}},"metrics":{"availableFields":["likes","retweets","replies","quotes","views","bookmarkCount"],"likes":145,"retweets":18,"replies":15,"quotes":7,"views":33526,"bookmarkCount":133},"media":[],"expandedUrl":null,"isRetweet":false,"isReply":false,"isQuote":false,"source":null,"communityId":null,"hasAIGeneratedMedia":false,"isPaidPromotion":false,"isTranslatable":false,"hasBirdwatchNotes":false,"possiblySensitive":false,"entities":{"hashtags":[{"text":"CollegeSoccer"}],"userMentions":[{"handle":"SRUSA_Official","displayName":"SRUSA - College Soccer Recruiting Agency 🇺🇸","platformUserId":"277570749"}],"urls":[],"symbols":[]},"card":null,"poll":null,"article":null,"place":null,"communityNote":null,"isEdited":false,"quotedTweet":null,"retweetedTweet":null},{"id":"1965782069323141355","url":"https://x.com/CRSportsLive/status/1965782069323141355","text":"Let me give you parents some recruiting advice.. When attending these college camps, make sure that you make a “connection” with at least one coach otherwise you’re just going to be going unless hes already a known recruit that they’re after. Also, if you knowwwwww your son is not SEC caliber or on that level then dont attend and get disappointed when they don’t see value in your child…. Attend the camps that’s your child’s level. If hes a lineman not above 6 ft 2, then attending an SEC camp is wasting time unless you just wanna go one time just say you (parent) met this and that coach. You have to be realistic about your son’s ability. man","createdAt":"2025-09-10T14:19:02.000Z","createdAtUnix":1757513942,"createdAtLabel":null,"language":"en","conversationId":"1965782069323141355","inReplyToStatusId":null,"inReplyToUserId":null,"inReplyToScreenName":null,"quotedStatusId":null,"retweetTweetId":null,"author":{"handle":"CRSportsLive","displayName":"Coach Reggie","avatarUrl":"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2110458449494478848/YeCKbt0N_400x400.jpg","profileUrl":"https://x.com/CRSportsLive","verified":false,"blueVerified":true,"platformUserId":"1343594281903284225","bio":"Head Football Coach of Jacksonville HS in Arkansas. Murray St. Alum. Former NFL player with the Cowboys, Lions & Cardinals. #ΚΑΨ ♦️♦️♦️#NupeSwag","location":"Little Rock, AR","website":null,"bannerUrl":"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/1343594281903284225/1788839375/1500x500","accountCreatedAt":"2020-12-28T16:27:05.000Z","privateAccount":false,"verifiedType":null,"affiliateLabel":null,"professional":{"type":"Business","category":[],"restId":"1846968902078591048"},"metrics":{"availableFields":["followers","following","tweets","favourites","listedCount","mediaCount"],"followers":3555,"following":1791,"tweets":2774,"favourites":1088,"listedCount":1,"mediaCount":1073}},"metrics":{"availableFields":["likes","retweets","replies","quotes","views","bookmarkCount"],"likes":37,"retweets":4,"replies":0,"quotes":0,"views":3590,"bookmarkCount":1},"media":[],"expandedUrl":null,"isRetweet":false,"isReply":false,"isQuote":false,"source":"Twitter for iPhone","communityId":null,"hasAIGeneratedMedia":false,"isPaidPromotion":false,"isTranslatable":false,"hasBirdwatchNotes":false,"possiblySensitive":false,"entities":{"hashtags":[],"userMentions":[],"urls":[],"symbols":[]},"card":null,"poll":null,"article":null,"place":null,"communityNote":null,"isEdited":false,"quotedTweet":null,"retweetedTweet":null},{"id":"2111874823357894824","url":"https://x.com/pmg911/status/2111874823357894824","text":"Dear AAU Parents,\n\nPlease take a little advice from a parent who has been around AAU basketball as a Coach & parent for 20+ years.\n\nStop chasing imaginary rankings from paid services\nlike PGH and cool social media posts from programs that over hype players on socials because that is all they can offer. Don't get caught up with trainers who are only worried about your children when they are in their gym.\n\nAsk real questions of program directors about approach on player development,\ncollege relationships and track record of getting players to college programs. Ask directors about recruiting plans for their players. Pay attention to programs that retain players and are not out recruiting over entire rosters year over year. Track record & trust between families & programs matters; especially in a rapidly changing recruiting landscape, you better be with a program that is committed to all their players and not just a few high profile girls.\n\nThe top of EVERY circuit has really good players/teams but the bottom of EVERY circuit has bad teams too. Being on an EYBL or 3SSB team, and playing 6-8 mpg can really hurt your recruitment. Not every program is a fit for every player/family but PLEASE do your homework!!\n\nHave honest discussions about potential level of play in college and where your child might fit. Be very weary of anyone who only talks about D1.\n\nWinning games in AAU is nice and hopefully your daughter is competitive and wants to win but it ultimately doesn't mean anything and not many college coaches are paying attention to the score unless one team is getting smoked. In fact, a coach might pay more attention to how your daughter is acting as a player when they are losing vs how they are playing in a 25pt win.\n\nGood luck to all as the girls get prepared for the High School season.\n\n@nj_panthers @CoachJordanNJP @unitedNJaau @ShoreshotsGirls @newjerseyrise @ESBC_BlueFlames @NJLadiesHoops @TinyGreenNBS \n@coachschoiceusa","createdAt":"2026-10-18T17:39:29.000Z","createdAtUnix":1792345169,"createdAtLabel":null,"language":"en","conversationId":"2111874823357894824","inReplyToStatusId":null,"inReplyToUserId":null,"inReplyToScreenName":null,"quotedStatusI